#CHLOEAI:1
TYPE="path_rules"
GLOB="docs/**, README.md"

PURPOSE:
Rules active when touching documentation files. Loaded on demand. Fill in the
ownership table for this project as docs accumulate.

---

AUDIENCE:
- docs/ is project reference: design intent, contracts, roadmaps, phase briefs.
- README.md is the GitHub-facing introduction for human readers.
- Engineering audience: future-you, future-AI sessions, external contributors.

---

FORMAT_CONVENTIONS:
- Markdown only. No HTML in doc files except where unavoidable (e.g., complex tables).
- Sentence case headings, not title case.
- Fenced code blocks with language hints for any code samples.
- Soft 100-char line wrap for diff readability. Do not reflow existing docs uninvited.
- Mark each new doc with a status header at top: ACTIVE | FROZEN | SUPERSEDED-BY-<path>

---

DOC_OWNERSHIP:

Fill in this table as docs accumulate. Status markers:
- ACTIVE          — current, actively maintained
- FROZEN          — historical record, do not edit
- SUPERSEDED-BY-X — replaced; X is the path of the replacement

| File | Owner | Status | Last reviewed | Rules |
|------|-------|--------|---------------|-------|
| `README.md` | Public-facing | ACTIVE | (date) | Keep brief and accurate. Status should mirror readme_AI.chloeai STATUS field. |
| `docs/project-brief.md` | Project (authoritative) | ACTIVE | (date) | Source of truth for project identity + invariants. Mark superseded clauses SUPERSEDED rather than deleting. |
| `docs/roadmap.md` | Project (authoritative) | ACTIVE | (date) | High-level roadmap. Update phase status as milestones close. |
| `docs/phase-N-brief.md` | Frozen archive | FROZEN | (date) | Historical phase brief. Do not edit. |

---

NEW_DOC_GUIDELINES:
- New design docs go in docs/ with kebab-case-name.md filename.
- Mark the doc's status at top: `**Status:** ACTIVE | FROZEN | SUPERSEDED-BY-<path>`
- Reference any related DEC-NNN, EXP-NNN, or THR-NNN by ID in the body to cross-link with continuity files.
- Add a row to the DOC_OWNERSHIP table above.

---

DO_NOT:
- Do not duplicate continuity content (THREADS, EXPERIMENTS, DECISIONS) into docs/. Continuity lives in ai_context/.
- Do not rewrite frozen archive docs to "update" them. If new direction conflicts, create a new doc and mark the old one SUPERSEDED-BY-<new-doc>.
- Do not commit auto-generated documentation derived from source unless the generator is checked in and reproducible.
- Do not rename a doc that other docs reference without updating the references in the same commit.
